## 4. Docker vs Kubernetes

| Aspect | Docker | Kubernetes |
|--------|--------|------------|
| **Use Case** | Local dev, packaging | Production orchestration |
| **Scope** | Single host | Multi-node cluster |
| **Scaling** | Manual | Automated (HPA) |
| **Service Discovery** | Docker DNS | CoreDNS + Services |
| **Load Balancing** | Port mapping | ClusterIP, NodePort, LoadBalancer |
| **Rolling Updates** | docker-compose rebuild | RollingUpdate strategy |
| **Secrets** | Env vars, volumes | Native Secrets API |
| **Storage** | Volumes | PersistentVolumes, PVC |
| **Monitoring** | docker stats | Metrics Server, Prometheus |

### When to Use Docker Alone

- Local development environment
- Single container applications
- CI/CD build pipelines
- Small scale testing

### When to Use Kubernetes

- Production deployments
- Multi-container microservices
- Auto-scaling requirements
- High availability needs
- Multi-node clusters
- Complex networking requirements

